ualities in education, income, wealth, prestige, occupation, political power, and health in the U.S. and other rich countries. How much inequality exists and why is it rising in some places? Do we live in a class society (and what does that mean)? How do families, aspirations, schools, social networks, employers, neighborhoods, and government policies shape who gets ahead and who falls behind? Why are education, jobs, and income distributed unequally by race, immigrant status, and gender? Throughout the course, we\u2019ll discuss and evaluate evidence from administrative data, surveys, experiments, and qualitative studies.", "catalogBreadth": null, "catalogDistr": null, "catalogEnrollmentPriority": "", "catalogLang": null, "catalogForbiddenOverlaps": null, "catalogAttribute": null, "catalogWhenOffered": null, "catalogComments": null, "catalogPrereqCoreq": null, "catalogPrereq": "", "catalogCoreq": "", "catalogFee": null, "catalogSatisfiesReq": null, "catalogPermission": null, "catalogCourseSubfield": null, "catalogOutcomes": null, "acadCareer": "UG", "acadGroup": "AS", "catalogName": null, "catalogNextOffered": null, "lastTermsOffered": "2026SU, 2026SP, 2025SP, 2024SP", "catalogCredits": null, "catalogGradeOption": null, "catalogLocation": null, "catalogCrosslisted": null, "catalogCrosslistings": null, "catalogComeets": null, "exploreCriteriaIds": []}, {"strm": 2930, "crseId": 366321, "crseOfferNbr": 2, "subject": "SOC", "catalogNbr": "3620", "titleShort": "Pop Controversies in Europe", "titleLong": "Population Controversies in Europe", "crseAttrs": [{"crseAttr": "0012", "crseAttrValue": "SBA-AG", "descr": "AG-Social & Behvl Analysis", "descrformal": "AG-Social and Behavioral Analysis", "attrDescr": "Distribution Requirements", "attrDescrShort": "DistReq"}, {"crseAttr": "0013", "crseAttrValue": "CU-ITL", "descr": "International Study", "descrformal": "International Study", "attrDescr": "Exploratory Studies", "attrDescrShort": "ExplStudy"}], "crseAttrValueGroups": [{